# Citation metadata — GitHub renders this as "Cite this repository".
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these measurements, please cite them as below and include the
  run identifier and ruleset version of the data file you used (numbers from
  different ruleset versions are not comparable). The sample frame builds on
  the Tranco list; please also cite the Tranco paper (see references).
type: dataset
title: "AI Discovery Radar — adoption measurements for machine-readable discovery and consent routes"
authors:
  # EIN Urheber (Entscheidung Florian, 15.09.2026 — ersetzt die Zwei-Autoren-Form
  # vom 02.09.). Die Firma steht in `affiliation`, nicht als zweiter Urheber:
  # Zenodos eigener Hinweis im Formular sagt „Use the Authors/Creators field for
  # names that should appear in the citation. Use the Contributors field below
  # for other names." Ein zweiter Eintrag OHNE ORCID bleibt in DataCite/OpenAIRE
  # ein loser Namensstring — Rohstoff fuer eine zweite Personen-Entitaet; die
  # Zitation zeigte ausserdem zwei Autoren fuer eine Person.
  #
  # Diese Datei ist die GitHub-Zitierkarte. Den Zenodo-Record baut `.zenodo.json`
  # — beide muessen dieselben Urheber nennen, sonst driften Repo und DOI.
  - family-names: "Berger"
    given-names: "Florian"
    affiliation: "Berger+Team"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5780-1147"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22178282  # concept DOI — always resolves to the latest version
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/flober81/ai-discovery-radar"
abstract: >-
  Monthly measurements of how many websites in a frozen, stratified sample
  (Tranco + Chrome UX Report country lists) actually publish machine-readable
  discovery and consent files such as robots.txt, llms.txt, TDMRep or
  agent-card.json. Shares are reported over observed hosts only, with Wilson
  95% intervals; the full ruleset, including its version history, is in
  RULESET.md. Each release carries two data files per month: the fixed
  1,000-source panel (trend) and the month's block of the wider frame
  (coverage); every file states its measurement window and completeness.
references:
  - type: report
    title: "AI Discovery Radar: measurement method and ruleset for tracking adoption of machine-readable discovery and consent routes (Technical Report v1.0)"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Berger"
        given-names: "Florian"
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5780-1147"
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22769680  # method report; concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22769679 resolves to the latest version
    notes: "Documents the classification model, denominator rule, sampling design and verification procedure behind this dataset."
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Tranco: A Research-Oriented Top Sites Ranking Hardened Against Manipulation"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Le Pochat"
        given-names: "Victor"
      - name: "et al."
    year: 2019
    conference:
      name: "NDSS 2019"
    url: "https://tranco-list.eu/"
